meta {
  name: tag: litellm metrics (stack)
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/litellm/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "stack",
    "stack_definition": {
      "restart_policy": "ordered",
      "secret_map": {
        "PG_PASSWORD": "${pods:random:32}",
        "MASTER_KEY": "${pods:random:32}"
      },
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "db",
          "image": "postgres:16",
          "description": "Postgres 16 - litellm spend/usage store. Every request's tokens + cost are written here per key/user/team/model; this is what the spend APIs and per-user accounting read. local_only.",
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "networking": {
            "default": { "protocol": "postgres", "port": 5432, "tapis_auth": false }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": { "exec_command": ["pg_isready", "-U", "litellm"] }
          },
          "environment_variables": {
            "POSTGRES_USER": "litellm",
            "POSTGRES_DB": "litellm",
            "POSTGRES_PASSWORD": "${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}"
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 250, "cpu_limit": 1000, "mem_request": 256, "mem_limit": 1024 }
        },
        {
          "name": "litellm",
          "image": "ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.81.3-stable",
          "description": "litellm proxy with usage tracking ON: Prometheus /metrics (callbacks: prometheus) + DB-backed spend per key/user/team/model. Set LITELLM_MASTER_KEY to manage keys and call the spend APIs. Poll /metrics (port 4000) or query /global/spend/report.",
          "depends_on": ["db"],
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "environment_variables": {
            "STORE_MODEL_IN_DB": "True",
            "DATABASE_URL": "postgresql://litellm:${stack:secrets:PG_PASSWORD}@${stack:db:host}:5432/litellm?sslmode=disable",
            "CONFIG_FILE_PATH": "/app/litellm.config.yaml",
            "LITELLM_MASTER_KEY": "sk-${stack:secrets:MASTER_KEY}"
          },
          "volume_mounts": {
            "/app/litellm.config.yaml": {
              "type": "ephemeral",
              "sub_path": "",
              "read_only": true,
              "config_content": "model_list: []\nlitellm_settings:\n  drop_params: true\n  # turns on the Prometheus /metrics endpoint (free, no enterprise license)\n  callbacks: [\"prometheus\"]\n  # add end_user label to the prometheus token/spend metrics (off by default for cardinality)\n  enable_end_user_cost_tracking_prometheus_only: true\ngeneral_settings:\n  store_model_in_db: true\n  # require a litellm key (not just tapis-auth) to read /metrics; comment out to scrape in-cluster without a key\n  # require_auth_for_metrics_endpoint: true\n",
              "config_permissions": "0644",
              "config_filename": "litellm.config.yaml",
              "config_update_mode": "always"
            }
          },
          "networking": {
            "default": {
              "protocol": "http",
              "port": 4000,
              "tapis_auth": true,
              "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
              "tapis_auth_return_path": "/",
              "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
              "tapis_ui_uri_description": "litellm proxy - swagger at /, metrics at /metrics, spend APIs under /global/spend",
              "proxy_compression": true,
              "proxy_compression_encodings": ["zstd", "br", "gzip"],
              "proxy_compression_min_response_body_bytes": 1024
            }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "http_get_path": "/health/readiness",
              "http_get_port": 4000,
              "initial_delay_seconds": 15,
              "period_seconds": 10,
              "failure_threshold": 6
            }
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 250, "cpu_limit": 1000, "mem_request": 256, "mem_limit": 1024 },
          "compute_queue": "default"
        }
      ]
    },
    "tag": "v1.81.3-metrics-stack",
    "commit_message": "litellm + postgres with usage tracking enabled: Prometheus /metrics (per model/user/team/key token + spend), end_user labels on, LITELLM_MASTER_KEY for key mgmt + spend APIs. Random shared PG + master key."
  }
}

docs {
  ## litellm with usage polling - per user / model / token / spend
  
  Same litellm + postgres pairing as `tag: litellm (stack)`, but with **usage tracking turned on**.
  The DB is what makes per-user/key/team accounting possible (already here); this tag adds the
  Prometheus endpoint + a master key.
  
  ### Two ways to grab usage
  **1) Prometheus `/metrics` (poll/scrape this)** - enabled via `callbacks: ["prometheus"]`.
  - `https://<litellm>.pods.<base>/metrics` (port 4000, same as the proxy).
  - Metrics: `litellm_total_tokens_metric`, `litellm_input_tokens_metric`,
    `litellm_output_tokens_metric`, `litellm_spend_metric` - each labeled
    `model, user, team, team_alias, api_key_alias, hashed_api_key, end_user, requested_model`.
  - **Free** - no enterprise license.
  
  **2) DB-backed spend APIs (query JSON)** - need the master key:
  - `GET /global/spend/report?...` - spend/tokens grouped by team / customer / internal user.
  - `GET /spend/logs` - per-request log rows.
  - `GET /user/info?user_id=...` - one user's totals + keys.
  Call with `Authorization: Bearer sk-<MASTER_KEY>` (read the `MASTER_KEY` stack secret).
  
  ### How litellm knows "who" (this is the header question)
  - **Virtual keys = the reliable way.** Issue a key per user/team:
    `POST /key/generate { "user_id": "alice", "team_id": "...", "models": [...] }`. Spend is tracked
    against that hashed key -> `user` / `team` / `api_key_alias` labels populate. Users call with
    *their* `sk-...` key.
  - **`user` body field** = the OpenAI `user` param, tracked as `end_user`. Convenient but
    **self-declared / spoofable** - fine for "which customer", not for trust.
  - **Headers do NOT set identity.** There's no `x-user` header. You can only *capture* arbitrary
    request headers as spend tags via `litellm_settings: extra_spend_tag_headers: ["x-team", ...]`
    for filtering - not for attribution. So: parse users via **keys**, not headers.
  
  ### Polling /metrics in practice (the tapis-auth wrinkle)
  `/metrics` shares port 4000, which is tapis-auth gated. So either:
  - **curl it with a Tapis JWT** through the public URL, or
  - **scrape it in-cluster** at `http://pods-<site>-<tenant>-<litellmPodId>:4000/metrics` (internal
    DNS bypasses Traefik/tapis-auth). Leave `require_auth_for_metrics_endpoint` commented so the
    in-cluster scrape needs no litellm key; uncomment it to force a key.
  
  ### Instantiate
  `POST /pods/stacks/from-template` with
  `{ "template": "litellm:v1.81.3-metrics-stack", "stack_id": "myllm",
     "pod_ids": { "litellm": "myllm" } }`
  then `POST /key/generate` (with the master key) to mint per-user keys and watch the labels fill.
  
  > Want it visualized? I can add **prometheus + grafana** members that scrape this and ship a
  > per-user/model token dashboard. One caveat: `${stack:litellm:host}` does NOT compile inside
  > `config_content` (only env/secret_map get stack-ref compilation), so the Prometheus scrape
  > target would be a placeholder you fill at instantiation (the litellm in-cluster host:port).
}
